{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This month for you, etc.</b> The reason for the repetition: ״רֹאשׁ חֳדָשִׁים רִאשׁוֹן הוּא״ and so forth — it intends to say that this month is a רֹאשׁ, meaning the choicest of the months, in the manner of what the verse says (Exodus 30:23): ״בְּשָׂמִים רֹאשׁ״." "And Scripture is precise in saying <b>for you</b>, for it is not the most praiseworthy and exalted of the months except for Israel. And you will find that our Sages of blessed memory said (Rosh HaShanah 11a): In Nisan they were redeemed, in Nisan they are destined to be redeemed — for the month is designated for Israel's benefit, and on this account ״רִאשׁוֹן הוּא״ — it is fitting for it to be yours, that you count from Nisan on account of its excellence." "Further, it alludes by saying <b>הַחֹדֶשׁ הַזֶּה</b> and not saying חֹדֶשׁ זֶה — to allude to the Known One, which is the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is written (Exodus 15:2): ״זֶה אֵלִי״; for this ״זֶה״ shall be ״for you״ — that He will reveal Himself to them, as they of blessed memory said (Mekhilta, Beshalach 14): a maidservant saw at the sea, etc." "Further, it alludes: <b>for this month is for you a רֹאשׁ</b> — meaning, that Israel shall be invested with the aspect of the head, that they shall no longer be despised and lowly. It further alludes in the word ״זֶה״ that it shall be a רֹאשׁ for all the months, which are twelve, corresponding to the numerical value of זֶה."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:48.936673467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}